Definition 14.3.1 (Scalar second fundamental form) . 168328A7D803 For a chosen unit normal $
u $ and local coordinate vectors $e_ i=\partial _ iF$, put \[  h_{ij}=\langle D_{e_ i}
u ,e_ jangle , \qquad A_ i{}^ j=g^{jk}h_{ik},\qquad H=\operatorname {tr}A.  \] Thus $h$ is positive on the outward-oriented round sphere, and the vector second fundamental form of Definition 7.1.1 is $B_{ij}=-h_{ij}
u $. We write $|A|^2=h_{ij}h^{ij}=|B|^2$. Raising an index in a time derivative requires differentiating $g^{ij}$ as well. This convention agrees with [ HP99 ] , Section 2.
